@startuml release_note_flow
' Flow: a release note from the pull request to the users' main menu.
' Preview: Alt+D (PlantUML extension)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

title Release note - from pull request to users

|Developer|
start
:Write notes/<key>.html in the holder module
<prefix>_release_notes, in the pull request of the change
(front matter: key, title, summary, tags, models;
HTML body with /web#action=<module>.<xml_id> buttons);

|Deploy|
:Merge, then -u <prefix>_release_notes;
:the holder's data file calls
_load_release_notes("<prefix>_release_notes"),
which reads the holder's notes/*.html;
if (key already in Odoo?) then (yes)
  :skip the file
(the note is never overwritten);
else (no)
  :create release.note
is_published = False
(visible to managers only);
endif
:Deployed by is set
= the user who ran the deploy;
:a demo video of the change
may be attached to the note;

|Deployer|
:open Release Notes > Unpublished,
read the note, watch the video,
press each button, check Models;
:press Publish;
if (current user = Deployed by
and at least one model?) then (yes)
  :is_published, Published by,
Published date set;
  :is_notified = True;
  :open web clients of the note's users
reload the announcement (bus);
else (no)
  |Deployer|
  :UserError, nothing published;
endif

|Users|
:the main menu icon counts the new notes;
the menu's panel names the newest
(only users who can read one of its models
and existed when it was published);
if (View or Skip?) then (View)
  :the newest note opens,
the pager walks the other new ones;
else (Skip)
endif
:the note is seen by that user
(opening it any other way counts too)
and no longer announced to them;
stop
@enduml
